# User-Level Access Control Implementation for FinSightRAG

## Overview
The current system has **no authentication/authorization layer**. Here's a comprehensive breakdown of what can be implemented:

---

## 1. AUTHENTICATION LAYER
### User Model & Authentication
- **User Registration & Login**
  - JWT token-based authentication
  - Password hashing (bcrypt)
  - Email verification
  - 2FA/MFA support

- **Session Management**
  - Token expiration (access + refresh tokens)
  - Device tracking
  - Login history

---

## 2. ROLE-BASED ACCESS CONTROL (RBAC)
### User Roles
```
- Admin
  ├─ View/Edit/Delete all data
  ├─ Manage users & permissions
  ├─ System configuration
  └─ Audit logs

- Analyst/Manager
  ├─ View assigned company data
  ├─ Create/Edit analysis
  ├─ Export reports
  └─ View team analytics

- Viewer/Stakeholder
  ├─ View-only access to assigned companies
  ├─ Limited to dashboards/reports
  └─ No data modification

- API User
  ├─ API key-based access
  ├─ Rate-limited endpoints
  └─ Audit logged
```

---

## 3. DATA-LEVEL ACCESS CONTROL
### Company Access Scoping
- **User-Company Mapping**
  - Users can be assigned to specific companies
  - Teams can manage multiple companies
  - Hierarchical access (parent company → subsidiaries)

- **Transcript Access**
  - Restrict by company
  - Restrict by year/quarter range
  - Restrict by document type

- **Sentiment/Chunk Access**
  - Inherit company permissions
  - Custom access rules per analysis

---

## 4. PERMISSION LEVELS
### Granular Permissions
```
Company Level:
  - company.view       → Read company data
  - company.create     → Create new company
  - company.edit       → Edit company metadata
  - company.delete     → Delete company (cascading)

Transcript Level:
  - transcript.view
  - transcript.create
  - transcript.edit
  - transcript.delete

Analysis Level:
  - analysis.view      → View sentiment analysis
  - analysis.create    → Run new analysis
  - analysis.edit      → Modify analysis parameters
  - analysis.export    → Export results

Vector Index Level:
  - index.view
  - index.regenerate
  - index.delete
```

---

## 5. ORGANIZATION/TEAM MANAGEMENT
### Multi-Tenant Structure
- **Organizations**
  - Separate data silos per organization
  - Organization admins
  - Subscription tiers/limits

- **Teams**
  - Sub-groups within organization
  - Team leads with delegation rights
  - Cross-team collaboration settings

- **Departments**
  - Finance, Operations, Strategy, etc.
  - Department-specific data access

---

## 6. AUDIT & COMPLIANCE
### Activity Logging
- User login/logout
- Data access logs
- Modification history (who/when/what changed)
- API request logs with IPs
- Failed access attempts

### Compliance Features
- Data retention policies
- GDPR compliance (data export/deletion)
- SOX compliance (for financial institutions)
- Change audit trails

---

## 7. API & RATE LIMITING
### API Key Management
- Generate/revoke API keys
- Scoped permissions per key
- Expiration dates
- Usage statistics

### Rate Limiting
- Per-user rate limits
- Per-API-key limits
- Burst protection
- Throttling by role

---

## 8. SECURITY FEATURES
### Additional Protections
- IP whitelisting (optional)
- Geographic restrictions
- Device fingerprinting
- Suspicious activity alerts
- Password policies (complexity, expiration)
- Account lockout after failed attempts
- Session invalidation on password change

---

## 9. DATA PRIVACY
### Privacy Controls
- Field-level masking (sensitive financial data)
- PII redaction in logs
- Data anonymization for exports
- Privacy policy acceptance tracking

---

## 10. DELEGATION & PROXY ACCESS
### Admin Functions
- Admin impersonation (with audit trail)
- Temporary access grants
- Delegation workflows

